6. **Unit cases.**
   - **`src/run/switch.rs`:**
     - the refusal order as one rstest table — five rungs, the first wins;
     - the pair resolution table: given, recorded, mixed;
     - the order of the appended lines, `launch` before the spawn and `window` after it when recorded.
   - **`crates/viola-pty`:**
     - a respawn swaps the child and the pump continues;
     - a child that ignores the signal reads `NotEnded` within the bound, through the injected clock;
     - a failed spawn ends the pump with the old exit.
   - Names `<subject>_<condition>_<expected>`. Keeps tests S2–S4 and S6.

- **Spec anchors:**
  - architecture: `decision/revive-pair-from-record`, `decision/launch-pair-handed-not-verified`,
    `decision/revive-resumes-in-place`, `decision/send-flight-lock`, `contract/event-data/launch` and
    `contract/instance-snapshot/launch`;
  - security-plan: `decision/new-listener-needs-log-entry`, `decision/launch-pair-kept-to-snapshot-and-event-log`,
    `decision/launch-pair-argv-crossing`, `decision/cli-frame-verbs-strict-modes-first` and
    `decision/adopt-signals-no-foreign-process`;
  - test-plan: `contract/viola-run-start/settings` and `decision/child-argv-read-from-proc`;
  - a11y-plan: `decision/time-bounds-never-on-human` and `decision/time-bounds-fall-on-the-driver`.

